{
 "title": "Caliptra Subsystem",
 "url": "https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-ss",
 "_note": [
  "Caliptra Subsystem (chipsalliance/caliptra-ss): the MCU (VeeR EL2), MCI, fuse",
  "and life-cycle controllers, I3C, and the integration around the Caliptra",
  "core.  caliptra-rtl, i3c-core and usb2 are vendored as submodules: the",
  "subsystem's RTL needs them to elaborate (roots), but only the subsystem's",
  "OWN modules are swept here (sweep_paths) -- the Caliptra core has its own",
  "chip sweep (sweep-caliptra.yml), and counting it twice would double the",
  "external-IP totals.  i3c-core and usb2 are swept as part of the subsystem",
  "(the subsystem is where they are integrated).",
  "",
  "always_srcs: the caliptra_prim packages and the generic prim library, which",
  "modules reach only through included .svh files the identifier-scan closure",
  "cannot see (caliptra_prim_ram_1p_pkg behind caliptra_prim_assert.svh).",
  "",
  "opentitan (lowRISC, pinned): the subsystem vendors OpenTitan's ast/, pwrmgr/,",
  "sensor_ctrl, tlul_adapter_dmi... but NOT the prim library they instantiate",
  "(prim_clock_buf, prim_flop_2sync, prim_pkg, prim_mubi_pkg, the",
  "`PRIM_FLOP_SPARSE_FSM macros).  Those modules could not be built by ANY",
  "tool -- the rows said nothing about any frontend.  The library comes from the",
  "OpenTitan checkout (prim/ + prim_generic/, with its real prim_assert.sv",
  "header, which reduces every macro to nothing under SYNTHESIS), so that a",
  "frontend failure on them is the frontend's and not the closure's.",
  "",
  "harness_roots/exclude_srcs: stubs/prim_pkg.sv is the legacy prim_pkg (with",
  "impl_e) the vendored ast/*_pgd.sv files expect; the checkout's prim_pkg is",
  "excluded.  unit_imports: the design's own filelists compile",
  "caliptra_prim_mubi4_sync.sv (file-scope `import caliptra_prim_mubi_pkg::*;`)",
  "ahead of modules that write a bare MuBi4True / mubi8_t -- the closure gets",
  "the same $unit import."
 ],
